%T A401472 14,14,15,16,16,16,16,16,17,17,17,17,18,18,19
%N A401472 Maximum size of a subset of {1, ..., n} whose subset products are all distinct.
%C A401472 This is g(n) in Erdős Problem 795.
%H A401472 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/795">Erdős Problem 795</a>, Erdős Problems.
%F A401472 a(n-1) <= a(n) <= a(n-1) + 1 for n >= 2.
%F A401472 If p is prime, a(p) = a(p-1) + 1.
%e A401472 a(6) = 4, attained by {2, 3, 4, 5}, whose subset products are 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 15, 20, 24, 30, 40, 60, 120.
%Y A401472 Cf. A000720.
%K A401472 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401472 1,3
